  "about": [
    "I build things that sit on both sides of the hardware/software line. On the metal side that means register-level drivers with no vendor HAL — configuring clocks, timers, NVIC and UART directly out of the datasheet — and synthesizable SystemVerilog on FPGA, where a design isn't done until static timing says it is.",
    "On the software side it means shipping. I've designed, built and deployed two production AI platforms end to end: data model and row-level-security auth, the product surface, and the deploy pipeline. Same instinct in both worlds — understand the layer underneath instead of trusting the abstraction.",
    "I'm finishing my B.E. in Computer Engineering at UT Arlington (May 2027) and looking for a Summer 2026 engineering internship where I can work close to the hardware, the systems, or both."
